{
  "about": "The waiting fields (amendment, Contract shapes), read by Bodies.waiting (Kotlin) and parseWaitingFields (TS). env is the build's. expected null means unreadable. Kotlin reads label..pollSeconds and skips jsOnly rows; TS also reads code, heartbeatUrl and startUrl, which only it keeps, and skips kotlinOnly rows, which are shaped as a beat's answer (capture-beat.v1 $defs.answer): only Kotlin reads those. Every other row is shaped as capture-descriptor.v1's waiting branch. A field absent or null where the schema allows it is null; a field of the wrong type, or outside the schema's bounds, makes the whole unreadable (a length counts characters, that is code points, as JSON Schema counts them); an overlayUrl off the build's Seazn host is dropped alone. Change only with both.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "every field",
      "env": "staging",
      "fields": {
        "code": "fx42hmnp7k2q",
        "label": "Example Town v Sample CC",
        "venueTimezone": "Europe/London",
        "scheduledStart": 1790003600,
        "autoAllowed": true,
        "destinationName": "YouTube · Example Town CC",
        "overlayUrl": "https://stg.seazn.club/overlay/fixtures/f1",
        "pollSeconds": 60,
        "heartbeatUrl": "https://stg.seazn.club/api/v1/capture/codes/fx42hmnp7k2q/beats",
        "startUrl": "https://stg.seazn.club/api/v1/capture/codes/fx42hmnp7k2q/start"
      },
      "expected": {
        "code": "fx42hmnp7k2q",
        "label": "Example Town v Sample CC",
        "venueTimezone": "Europe/London",
        "scheduledStart": 1790003600,
        "autoAllowed": true,
